Hi Nick,

I have some
doubts about the analysis that you call "pseudo-Bayesian" approach. I
want to know if an average Lnl value is obtained from all runs (corresponding
to all topologies). In this case, if there were several probable dispersion
routes (= several dispersion matrices), could I do a pseudo-Bayesian analysis
for each matrix (under the same model), estimate the AIC values from the mean
Lnl obtained and finally infer which route best fits with my data? Would it be
statistically correct?

Thank you in advance!

All the best

